summary:
- topic: Superintendent's Resignation
  text: The Board Chair announced Superintendent Timothy Metheny's resignation, effective
    December 5th, and assured the public that the board is working on a smooth transition
    plan for the district's next leader.
- topic: District Performance Highlights
  text: The Superintendent reported significant district-wide progress, including
    decreased chronic student absenteeism, a dramatic reduction in out-of-school suspensions
    at SPHS from 150 to 36, and SPHS SAT scores now exceeding the national average
    for the first time in over seven years.
- topic: Facilities Security Upgrades
  text: The Director of Operations announced that security cameras will be installed
    in all five elementary schools over the summer. Additionally, new secure vestibules
    will be constructed at Brown, Kaler, and Small elementary schools this summer,
    with Skillin and Dyer scheduled for summer 2026.
- topic: Staff Recognition
  text: The board honored Monica Malcolmson of Brown Elementary School as the 2025
    Cumberland County Teacher of the Year and celebrated nine district retirees with
    15 or more years of service, representing a collective 242 years of dedication.
- topic: Community Partnerships
  text: A comprehensive report highlighted the success of numerous community partnerships,
    including career exploration programs (ELOs), volunteer efforts, and significant
    donations from local businesses and organizations that support student enrichment.
- topic: Federal Funding Update
  text: The Assistant Superintendent reported an unanticipated decrease in federal
    ESEA Title I and Title IV funding for the upcoming fiscal year, which will primarily
    impact non-personnel budgets like professional development. Allocations for Title
    II and III are still pending.
- topic: Pre-K Expansion
  text: The district is moving forward with a partnership with Chickadee to fund 12
    pre-K seats for South Portland residents. A separate planned partnership with
    United Way for additional seats has been delayed until Fall 2026.
- topic: Budget Referendum
  text: The board and community members urged the public to vote in support of the
    school budget at the referendum scheduled for the following day.
